  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $N-\\lambda I:$\n\ufeff\ufeff\ufeff\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(N-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda +\\sqrt{7}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal.",
